  mycomment   = {I thought this was a fun little idea: by randomly initializing networks and then killing the right edges, one can get good networks. And they are sparser! This is essentially the "lottery ticket hypothesis" by [Frankle and Carbin, *The lottery ticket hypothesis: Finding sparse, trainable neural networks* (2018)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.03635).}
}

